# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data. None of this belongs in the repository: the photos are large (a single
# corpus here is 160 MB+), they are unpublished experimental data, and the
# derived files are all reproducible from them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Spotting Assays/
Old/
*.JPG
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.tif
*.tiff

# Measurement cache and per-folder answers
.spotting_cache/
spotting_config.json
timecourse_config.json

# Experiment files. They name real strains and record an ABSOLUTE path to the
# photo folder on the machine that made them, which is exactly what commit
# 6931a62 ("Remove hardcoded local paths from tracked files") set out to keep
# out of the repository. Plate templates stay tracked: those are strain-free
# geometry and are meant to be shared.
Experiment Designs/

# Everything a run produces
Results/
timecourse_candidates.csv
*.pptx
*.xlsx

# The packaged program is ~150 MB and reproducible with build_exe.py. Publish
# it as a release download, not a commit. spotting_error.log is what a crashed
# window leaves behind.
*.exe
spotting_error.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# R
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local tooling config: machine-specific paths, of no use to anyone else.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/

# Where the review window found each set's photographs on THIS machine. The
# reviews themselves live in Results/ (already ignored) and record their own
# capture folder, so nothing is lost by leaving this out.
.results_review_links.json
review_error.log
